<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  robot: mirror_hand_1013
  consumers: CAD Viewer / robot_state_publisher; source for the enclosed-hand USD
  units: metres, kilograms, seconds, radians; mesh source units: millimetres
  root: palm_link at the existing Right_Hand_0816.iam root origin, right-handed
  frame exception: existing Inventor assembly axes retained; no REP-103 remapping
  source: urdf_axes/current_geometry.json, joint_axes.json, fourbar_geometry.json;
          Current_Assembly.step plus Palm_Cover.step and Dorsal_Cover.step
  canonical artifact: this directly authored XML; no URDF regeneration pipeline

  Link ledger (all 23 links are physical; all mesh origins are identity):
  - palm_link: root; fixed hand plate, finger frames, motor cases and fasteners.
  - fingerN_gimbal_link: N=1..5; origin measured P0, axes of current Gimbal.ipt;
    child of fingerN_abduction_joint; contains the corresponding gimbal.
  - fingerN_proximal_link: P0 with same zero axes; child of fingerN_flexion_joint;
    contains Proximal, Proximal_Shell and assigned rigid fasteners.
  - fingerN_distal_link: P2 with same zero axes; child of fingerN_distal_joint;
    contains Distal, Distal_Shell and assigned rigid fasteners.
  - fingerN_link_link: P1 with same zero axes; child of fingerN_link_joint;
    contains the independent four-bar Link and assigned rigid fasteners.
  - palm_cover_link / dorsal_cover_link: assembly-root frame; fixed to palm_link;
    latest two-piece simple-oval palm enclosure.
  - Geometry: meshes/LINK_NAME.stl, exported directly into the owning link frame;
    visual and collision share identity origins and scale 0.001 0.001 0.001.
  - Inertial source: asset_manifest.json, CAD solid mass-property integration;
    COM in link coordinates, full inertia about COM aligned with link axes.

  Joint ledger:
  - fingerN_abduction_joint: palm to gimbal, measured assembly centre/rpy;
    axis +Z of measured gimbal; positive follows the right-hand rule.
    Outward/inward naming and motor signs have not been calibrated.
  - fingerN_flexion_joint: gimbal to proximal at P0, axis local -X;
    positive reduces the proximal YZ-plane angle and bends the finger.
  - fingerN_distal_joint: proximal to distal at P2, passive axis local -X.
  - fingerN_link_joint: gimbal to Link at P1=(0,0,-0.006), passive axis local -X.
  - Covers use fixed identity joints. Joint zero is the current CAD pose,
    not an independently calibrated motor-zero or straight-finger pose.

  Mechanism ledger:
  - Five fingers, two commanded OUTPUT coordinates per finger: 10 commanded DoF.
  - This plain URDF is a tree with 20 rotary joints. Five Link-to-Distal closure
    hinges at P3 MUST be added by the USD workflow to enforce the actual mechanism.
  - Measured four-bar lengths: P0-P2=52, P1-P3=50.5, P2-P3=6, P0-P1=6 mm.
  - No linear mimic is specified: distal coupling is nonlinear. For tree/viewer
    poses use tools/pose_fourbar.py; fourbar_geometry.json records closure frames.
  - Servo horns and ball rods are omitted from this reduced output-coordinate
    model. Motor cases remain fixed. Direct root actuation replaces their drive
    mapping; this is not a simulation of the full two-servo ball-link mechanism.

  Assumptions and provisional parameters:
  - Uniform density 1200 kg/m^3 for every CAD solid, including mixed materials;
    mass and inertia are estimates, not weighed/calibrated hardware parameters.
  - Small fasteners are assigned to the nearest principal-part bounding volume
    (AABB distance, centre-distance tie break); this approximates rigid ownership,
    including at shared pin axes. Principal-part membership is explicit.
  - Limits updated 2026-10-13 from the user's dimensioned mechanism image:
    abduction [-20,+20] deg, proximal flexion [0,86] deg, distal [0,80] deg.
    Applied to all five fingers, taking the existing open CAD pose as zero;
    motor-zero calibration is still independent. Effort 0.25 N m and velocity
    1 rad/s remain provisional. The pictured 6, 13.5 and lower 20 deg installation
    angles do not replace the measured assembly transforms.
  - Distal remains passive: at proximal 86 deg the current CAD four-bar yields
    approximately 71.2405 deg distal. An 80 deg stop is not a mimic target.
    The passive Link hinge retains [-pi,pi], effort 0, velocity 2 rad/s.
    USD closures, not an extra passive drive, determine passive motion.
  - Drive gains are external to this URDF.
  - Collision meshes match visuals here. USD must select an appropriate explicit
    convex decomposition; triangle meshes are not certified dynamic colliders.
-->
